{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794880132,"nonce":"kd720FrJvv7FJfRndUIUZ7PSzTc=","message":"Repeatable check for the Alt+letter report (tested against cf925af, fs-blinc-3.1).\n\nThe test feeds the same event sequence the window produces into a real Blinc text input (the TextInput widget inside a small dialog) and into an on_key_down hook on the root element. For a key press with a character the window sends TEXT_INPUT first, then KEY_DOWN; the only chords left out of TEXT_INPUT are Ctrl without AltGr, and Meta.\n\nResult at cf925af:\n- Alt+F (character 'f', code 70, alt = true): the text field now contains \"f\". The hook sees (code 70, alt = true) only after the character is already in the field.\n- Ctrl+F and Meta+F: nothing is typed, the hook sees both presses.\n- Plain F: \"f\" is typed (control case).\n\nWhere the behaviour comes from:\n- crates/blinc_app/src/windowed/event_loop/input/keyboard.rs:244-259 (cf925af) builds TEXT_INPUT unless Ctrl (without AltGr) or Meta is held; Alt is not tested. On project-blinc/Blinc main (67f54d2) the same condition is at :238-251 (`if !mods.ctrl \u0026\u0026 !mods.meta`).\n- crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input/handlers.rs:373 and crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_area/handlers.rs:250-251 skip TEXT_INPUT only for ctx.ctrl or ctx.meta; ctx.alt is never read (identical on cf925af and main).\n\nWhat the test does not show: whether winit delivers text for Alt+letter on Windows or macOS. At cf925af the character comes from the platform text (keyboard.rs:84-85); on main it comes from the key itself (keyboard.rs:82), so Alt+F gives 'f' there on every platform. We expect the platform text for Alt+F to be \"f\" on X11 and Wayland but have not measured it, and we have not run it on Windows or macOS.\n\nWhy it matters: a menu bar that opens with Alt+F (mnemonic) inserts an \"f\" into a focused text field, and the shortcut handler runs after the character.\n\nThe test is a plain cargo test (no window): fs-components-widgets/tests/alt_letter_spike.rs in the branch unreviewed/components-menue-m2 of FreeSynergy/fs-components (commit d08bdbb9). It uses the public broadcast_text_input_event and broadcast_key_event of RenderTree. Test names: alt_letter_is_typed_into_the_field_and_reaches_the_hook_after_it, ctrl_and_meta_letters_are_not_typed, a_plain_letter_is_typed.","files":null}]}